(vector (map (:db/id -1)
  (:adr/id "2607231855")
  (:adr/title "Shinshi Kaizen Standing-Tick: Self-Hosted Infra Attempt (murakumo.cloud / git.kotobase.net) — Findings, Shipped Work, and Remaining Gap")
  (:adr/status "accepted")
  (:adr/date "2026-07-23")
  (:adr/deciders (vector "Jun Kawasaki"))
  (:adr/type "decision-record")
  (:adr/body "
## Summary

Attempted to replace claude.ai's cloud routine (RemoteTrigger, 403'd on the
jk-luxury org) and a Mac LaunchAgent fallback with a fully self-hosted daily
kaizen-reconciliation tick for jk-luxury/club-shinshi-app's progress/BMC
snapshot (docs/260613-progress.{datoms.edn,clj} + docs/260613-bmc-lean.
{datoms.edn,clj} — the artifact ADR-2606131400 in jk-luxury/club-shinshi
declares authoritative), running on murakumo.cloud (LLM backend) and
git.kotobase.net (repo host, replacing a GitHub PAT dependency).

**Net result:** murakumo.cloud as an LLM backend works and a Cloudflare
Cron Trigger + tick implementation was built for it (not yet deployed,
blocked on a GitHub write credential). git.kotobase.net turned out to
require a full self-sovereign git-push protocol for ANY write — assessed
as disproportionate for this use case, so that direction is PAUSED, not
completed. One genuinely valuable piece of shared infra WAS shipped and
deployed as a side effect: a private-repo read gate on the real
git.kotobase.net Worker, previously 100% publicly readable with no way to
host anything confidential there.

## Context

- claude.ai's `RemoteTrigger` cloud-routine API returned 403 for
  jk-luxury/club-shinshi-app — no GitHub App/org authorization for that
  org on the cloud-routine surface. Same wall as ADR-2607172900
  (cloud-itonami / itonami-qwen36-tick).
- A session-local `CronCreate` job and a Mac `launchd` LaunchAgent
  (`~/.gftd/run-shinshi-kaizen-tick.cljs`, `com.gftd.shinshi-kaizen-tick`
  plist) were both built as working fallbacks — both are Mac-uptime-
  dependent, which prompted the request to self-host the recurring tick
  on murakumo.cloud instead.
- The user explicitly rejected a GitHub fine-grained PAT for the write
  path (long-lived, personal-account-tied, sits as a raw secret in a
  Worker) and asked to avoid GitHub Actions too, preferring the tick's
  execution and repo-write both live on owned infra (murakumo.cloud /
  git.kotobase.net).

## Investigation and findings

### murakumo.cloud (`gftdcojp/cloud-murakumo`)

No pre-existing scheduling/routine-hosting capability — purely a static
SPA + LLM inference reverse-proxy Worker (`site_worker.cljs`) + Stripe
checkout + x402 billing. No Cron Trigger, no Durable Object, no
consumer-registry pattern existed.

**Built** (branch `feat/shinshi-kaizen-scheduled-tick`, pushed, NOT yet
merged/deployed): `cloud_murakumo/shinshi_kaizen.cljs` — a `scheduled()`
Cloudflare Cron Trigger handler wired into `site_worker.cljs`'s default
export alongside the existing `fetch` handler. Design: ONE single-shot
LLM completion per tick (not an agentic tool loop) against
`MURAKUMO_OPENAI_URL` (the same upstream this Worker already proxies),
given the current 4 file contents + a GitHub commit-log-since-last-check,
asked to answer `NO_DRIFT` or full replacement file contents in a
`===FILE: path===...===END===` wire format. Guardrails ported from the
LaunchAgent prototype: size-deviation (>50%), missing `kaizen-verified`
header marker, and a hand-written balanced-bracket parser — any failure
aborts the WHOLE tick, nothing written. Repo I/O originally targeted the
GitHub REST + Git Data API (blob/tree/commit/branch/merge, atomic
multi-file commit) — this is the part blocked on a write credential
(the rejected PAT). Verified: shadow-cljs release build clean (0
warnings), `wrangler deploy --dry-run` parses config and bundles. NOT
deployed — `wrangler.jsonc`'s `triggers.crons: [\"13 0 * * *\"]` addition
and the GITHUB_TOKEN secret requirement are both still only on the
feature branch.

### git.kotobase.net — two non-overlapping systems discovered

1. **`kotobase.protocols.git`** (pure lib in `kotoba-lang/kotobase-protocols`,
   `src/kotobase/protocols/git.cljc`) — dumb-HTTP only (`GET`/`PUT` on
   `info/refs`, `HEAD`, `objects/{2}/{38}`), no sha1 verification, no
   smart protocol. Deployed as part of `kotobase-protocols-worker`
   (canonical source now `gftdcojp/net-kotobase/protocols-worker`, the
   sibling repo `kotoba-lang/kotobase-protocols-worker` is explicitly
   marked retired in its own `package.json`). Confirmed via the
   Cloudflare API this Worker actually serves `s3.kotobase.net`,
   `atproto.kotobase.net`, and `pinning.kotobase.net` — **NOT**
   `git.kotobase.net`, despite that repo's `wrangler.jsonc` listing it as
   a route (a stale/wrong config entry).
2. **`kotobase-git`** (`worker/git-worker.mjs` in the SAME
   `kotoba-lang/kotobase-protocols` repo, no `wrangler.jsonc` existed for
   it) — this IS what `git.kotobase.net` actually routes to (confirmed
   via `GET /accounts/:id/workers/domains` on the Cloudflare API, and by
   the live `/health` response matching this file's exact JSON shape,
   which the other system doesn't even implement). Backed by D1
   (`repos`/`delegates`/`refs`/`objects`/`audit`/`event_outbox` tables —
   a genuine Radicle-shaped per-repo owner+delegate access-control data
   model), R2 (loose objects + CIDv1 canonical blocks), a KV namespace,
   and a `murakumo-kaizen` queue (interesting name — pre-existing,
   unrelated to this session's work, not investigated further).
   **Reads** (`gitRead`): zero auth, by design (dumb-HTTP \"clonable\").
   **Writes** (`/xrpc/kotobase.git.*`): gated first by a shared
   `ADMIN_TOKEN` bearer, then — unconditionally, not optional — by
   `kotoba-rad`-style Nekko Ed25519 request signing (`did:key`), a
   per-ref `sigref` signature, **quorum approval** (a CACAO delegation
   chain from the repo's `owner_did` down to each approving signer,
   verified against `delegates`), AND a live round-trip to kotobase.net's
   OWN separate Datomic XRPC endpoint
   (`ai.gftd.apps.kotobase.datomic.datoms`) to verify a matching
   `:git.ref/sigref` projection exists before the ref update is accepted.
   There is no simpler write path — `gitRead` has no `PUT` handler at
   all, unlike the other (non-git-serving) system.

### Decision: pause git.kotobase.net as the write target

Implementing the full Nekko/sigref/quorum/kotobase-projection protocol
client-side (did:key identity mint, CACAO delegation chain mint, per-ref
signing, a live kotobase.net datomic transact+query round-trip) purely to
let a daily 4-file reconciliation tick push a commit is disproportionate
— this protocol reads as infrastructure for a genuinely multi-party /
multi-agent governance scenario (`bounds: {maxFiles, maxChangedLines,
maxSpendUsd, allowedPhases}` fields visible in the ref-set event payload
strongly suggest an autonomous-agent-fleet governance system, not a
single trusted daily job). **Deferred, not abandoned** — if a second
consumer with a genuine multi-signer governance need shows up, this is
the right system to extend into. For now, jk-luxury/club-shinshi-app's
kaizen docs STAY on GitHub (not relocated to kotobase) — ADR-2606131400's
authority claim over `docs/260613-*` remains in force, unchanged by this
ADR.

## What WAS shipped (deployed to production, verified live)

**Private-repo read gate for `git.kotobase.net`** (`kotobase-git` Worker,
`kotoba-lang/kotobase-protocols` commit `331acf3`, merged to main): the
dumb-HTTP read surface had ZERO authentication for GET/HEAD on ANY
hosted repo (by original design — \"making it clonable\" per
`bin/seed_git.cljs`'s own docstring) prior to this change. This is a real
privacy exposure for anything confidential hosted there. Added
`PRIVATE_GIT_REPO_PREFIXES` (a plain, non-secret Worker var — comma-
separated `org/repo` names) + `isPrivateRepo()`/`privateRepoPrefixes()`:
a matching repo's GET/HEAD on `info/refs`/`HEAD`/`objects/{sha}` now
requires the same `ADMIN_TOKEN` bearer a write already needs. Every other
repo, and every non-git surface, is unaffected — boundary-tested (a repo
like `club-shinshi-kaizen-evil` does not false-positive match
`club-shinshi-kaizen`) and smoke-tested live post-deploy (health/other-
repos/write-gate unchanged; the one configured private repo now 401s
without a bearer, 404s — correctly past the gate — with a valid one).

The `PRIVATE_GIT_REPO_PREFIXES` list currently contains
`jk-luxury/club-shinshi-kaizen` (a placeholder repo name reserved for the
paused kotobase-native direction) — nothing is actually seeded there
yet, since the write-path decision above means this repo was never
populated. The gate itself is real, live, and immediately reusable for
any FUTURE confidential repo on this substrate without further work.

`net-kotobase/protocols-worker`'s `wrangler.jsonc` still lists
`git.kotobase.net` as a route despite not actually owning that hostname —
flagged here as a known-stale config entry (not touched further in this
ADR's scope; an identical read-gate mistakenly added there was cleanly
reverted, commit `6e1f4a6` in `gftdcojp/net-kotobase`, once the
Cloudflare API confirmed the real routing target).

**`ADMIN_TOKEN` on `kotobase-git` was rotated** (old value was
unrecoverable — Cloudflare secrets are write-only and it wasn't in
Keychain/kagi under any name checked) — new value stored in kagi
(compartment `net-kotobase`, item `KOTOBASE_GIT_ADMIN_TOKEN`) and
mirrored to Keychain (`kotobase-git:ADMIN_TOKEN`). **Any other consumer
of the old `ADMIN_TOKEN` value is now broken** and needs the new one —
not verified whether any existed; this is the one real risk this ADR
knowingly accepted (user explicit call: rotate now, unknown blast radius
accepted).

## Current gap (nothing standing/live for the actual kaizen tick today)

1. No cloud-hosted recurring kaizen tick is currently running anywhere
   (the Mac LaunchAgent from ADR-2607172900's pattern was built earlier
   this session as `com.gftd.shinshi-kaizen-tick` + a session `CronCreate`
   job, but the CronCreate job was explicitly cancelled once the
   murakumo.cloud direction was chosen — the LaunchAgent's live status
   was not re-verified at ADR-writing time).
2. `cloud-murakumo`'s `feat/shinshi-kaizen-scheduled-tick` branch has a
   working, build-verified Cron Trigger tick, but it targets the GitHub
   REST/Git-Data API for writes and has no credential to use (PAT
   rejected; GitHub App and GitHub Actions-native alternatives were
   proposed but neither was chosen/built before the git.kotobase.net
   detour started).
3. The git.kotobase.net direction is paused per the decision above — no
   further work will land there for THIS use case unless revisited.

## Recommendation (not yet actioned)

Pick up the GitHub-credential decision that was interrupted by the
git.kotobase.net detour: either (a) a GitHub App (short-lived
installation tokens, no long-lived PAT, still satisfies \"no PAT\") for
`cloud-murakumo`'s already-built tick, or (b) move the tick logic into a
`.github/workflows/*.yml` scheduled workflow inside
jk-luxury/club-shinshi-app itself (GitHub Actions' automatic
per-run-scoped `GITHUB_TOKEN`, zero stored credential at all, but the
execution host is GitHub Actions rather than murakumo.cloud). Both were
on the table before this ADR's detour and remain the live options.
")))
